    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1221">

                <pb facs="0859" n="743" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg743"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812,512/295.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Consul General Hanna.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-06-26T17:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 26, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Consul, Tampico, reports that customs authorities are forcing oil companies to
                    pay taxes Mexican gold, or American gold at two for one when exchange is three
                    for one, and that they refuse to accept Carrancista currency bills although
                    these made legal tender by decrees April 1913 and February 1914.</p>
                <p>Bring to attention of Carranza and request that orders be given for relief from
                    this manifestly unjust action.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
